<title>USA: SENSORMATIC TO SELL DIVISION.</title>
<headline>SENSORMATIC TO SELL DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Security systems company Sensormatic Electronics Corp said on Monday that it had signed a letter of intent to sell its U.S. Enterprise Accounts Division to Security Technologies Inc, a privately held security company based in Coral Gables, Florida.</p>
<p>Terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Sensormatic chief executive Robert Vanourek said the company was committed to selling the division to harmonize distribution channels.</p>
<p>Security Technologies' largest shareholder is Jules Kroll of Kroll Associates, with minority interests held by MCI Communications.</p>
</text>
